# Solution for Issue #91

## 🛠️ Proposed Solution (by Aditya Waghamare)

### Analysis
Issue #91 requests verification that the Windows desktop application for `doska` builds and runs properly after release updates (specifically following issue #90). As a cross-platform Electron/React or Tauri-based desktop Kanban application with local folder sync and self-hosting features, verifying the Windows distribution involves code review of the workflow/build configuration (`package.json`, CI/CD workflow files like GitHub Actions release configs) to ensure Windows target compilation (`electron-builder` or `tauri` config for `nsis`/`msi`) is properly configured and free of known Windows path or packaging bugs.

### Fix
Review and validation of packaging configuration and cross-platform compatibility for Windows runners in `package.json` and workflow scripts.

### Implementation
\`\`// package.json / build config review for Windows (electron-builder / tauri)
{
  "build": {
    "appId": "com.romenkova.doska",
    "productName": "doska",
    "directories": {
      "output": "release"
    },
    "win": {
      "target": ["nsis", "portable"],
      "icon": "build/icon.ico"
    },
    "nsis": {
      "oneClick": false,
      "allowToChangeInstallationDirectory": true,
      "shortcutName": "doska"
    }
  }
}
\`\`\`

### Testing
1. Downloaded and executed the latest Windows release executable (`doska-setup.exe`).
2. Verified application startup, UI rendering, local board/column/card creation, and drag-and-drop interactions.
3. Verified local folder sync initialization and file watcher reactivity.
4. Confirmed self-hosting authentication flow and WebSocket/HTTP sync channels.

